IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc3-order-18-general`

-- Tests for Order 18, Division 1, rules 1 to 14 (src lines 1696-1816).  Expected values are written
-- from the text, decided before running.

-- Rule 1
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(i) an appeal from a decision made on an application in an action` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(iv a) an appeal from a decision made by a District Judge or Magistrate in a hearing on the merits of an originating application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(v) an appeal from a decision of an appellate Court on an application by summons in an appeal under this Order or Order 19` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 18 r 1(1)(b) an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal to the appellate Court under this Order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceeding` `o 18 r 1(1) any other proceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(2) the application is an application in an action` `o 18 r 1(2)(a)(i) an application taken out after the action is commenced` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(2) the application is an application in an action` `o 18 r 1(2)(a)(iii) an application for the enforcement of the judgment or order` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(2) the application is an application in an action` `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(i) an application taken out or heard on the same day as the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application, or at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the judgment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(2) the application is an application in an action` `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(i) an application taken out or heard on the same day as the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application, or at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the judgment` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the exception for paragraph (1)(a)(iv a) lifts the exclusion
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(2) the application is an application in an action` `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(ii) a matter under appeal which is within the scope of Order 19` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 1(2) the application is an application in an action` `o 18 r 1(2) any other application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Rule 2
#ASSERT `o 18 r 2(1) this Order gives way to a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 2(1) this Order gives way to a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 18 r 2 the Division of this Order that concerns the appeal` `o 18 r 2(2) an appeal from the Registrar to the District Judge in proceedings in the State Courts` EQUALS JUST `o 18 r 2(2) Division 2`
#ASSERT `o 18 r 2 the Division of this Order that concerns the appeal` `o 18 r 2(3) an appeal from the District Judge or Magistrate to the General Division` EQUALS JUST `o 18 r 2(3) Division 3`
#ASSERT `o 18 r 2 the Division of this Order that concerns the appeal` `o 18 r 2(4) an appeal from the Registrar to the Judge in proceedings in the General Division` EQUALS JUST `o 18 r 2(4) Division 4`
#ASSERT `o 18 r 2 the Division of this Order that concerns the appeal` `o 18 r 2 any other appeal` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Rule 3
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the period for the lower Court to determine costs`'s `period length` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the period for the lower Court to determine costs`'s `period unit` EQUALS Days
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the date after which the time starts to run where costs are not determined within 30 days` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026) -- costs not determined: 30 days after 1 March is 31 March
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the date after which the time starts to run where costs are not determined within 30 days` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 31 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING -- costs determined on the 30th day: determined within 30 days
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the date after which the time starts to run where costs are not determined within 30 days` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026) -- determined on day 31: not within 30 days
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the date after which the time starts to run where costs are not determined within 30 days` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (d): after the bar lifts the Rule does not itself say the time runs; the bar's own question is "is still barred from starting to run"
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- costs not yet determined: a flat negative
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a written law or paragraph (1A) or (2) provides otherwise
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the Court otherwise orders
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 18 r 3(2)(a)(i) decided on the parties' entitlement to costs, even if the amount of costs or disbursements has not been determined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 18 r 3(2)(a)(ii) ordered that costs be assessed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 18 r 3(2)(a)(iii) ordered that costs be reserved` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 18 r 3(2)(a)(iv) decided that there is to be no order as to costs or that each party is to bear its own costs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 18 r 3(2)(a) done something else on costs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(b) the time does not run until all the matters have been heard and determined` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(b) the time does not run until all the matters have been heard and determined` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(b) the time does not run until all the matters have been heard and determined` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- "subject to sub-paragraph (c)"
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c) paragraph (2)(c) applies to the single application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c) paragraph (2)(c) applies to the single application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c) paragraph (2)(c) applies to the single application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(i) the date after which the time runs for the appeal against the decision of the Registrar` TRUE (Date 4 5 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 4 5 2026)
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(i) the date after which the time runs for the appeal against the decision of the Registrar` FALSE (Date 4 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(ii) the date after which the time runs for an appeal or an application for permission against a decision on a matter heard before the Judge` TRUE (Date 11 5 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 5 2026)
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(ii) the date after which the time runs for an appeal or an application for permission against a decision on a matter heard before the Judge` FALSE (Date 11 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the date after which the time runs for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters` TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 12 5 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 12 5 2026) -- the Court affirmed, varied or set aside
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the date after which the time runs for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 13 5 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 13 5 2026) -- the Court certified no further arguments are required
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the date after which the time runs for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters` TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the date after which the time runs for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters` FALSE TRUE (JUST (Date 12 5 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- not a single application dealing with more than one matter
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the date after which the time runs for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters` TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 12 5 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING -- no request for further arguments
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal is still barred from starting to run` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- costs not yet determined: the bar holds (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (d))
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal is still barred from starting to run` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- determined: the bar has lifted (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (d))
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal is still barred from starting to run` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Court otherwise orders: the "unless" lifts the bar (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (d))
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal is still barred from starting to run` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a written law or paragraph (1A) or (2) provides otherwise (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (d))
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the time starts to run after the expiry of the 30-day period` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE -- costs not determined
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the time starts to run after the expiry of the 30-day period` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 31 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- costs determined on the 30th day: the "where" is not met
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the time starts to run after the expiry of the 30-day period` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- determined on day 31
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(1A) the time starts to run after the expiry of the 30-day period` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- determined within 30 days
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(b) the time is still barred from running because not all the matters have been heard and determined` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- single application, matters outstanding: the bar holds
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(b) the time is still barred from running because not all the matters have been heard and determined` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- all matters determined: the bar has lifted
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(b) the time is still barred from running because not all the matters have been heard and determined` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a single application dealing with more than one matter
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(b) the time is still barred from running because not all the matters have been heard and determined` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "subject to sub-paragraph (c)"
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(i) the time for the appeal against the decision of the Registrar runs when the Registrar has heard and determined all the matters to be heard before the Registrar` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(i) the time for the appeal against the decision of the Registrar runs when the Registrar has heard and determined all the matters to be heard before the Registrar` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a "where" that is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(ii) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against a decision on a matter heard before the Judge runs when the Judge has heard and determined all the matters before the Judge` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(c)(ii) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against a decision on a matter heard before the Judge runs when the Judge has heard and determined all the matters before the Judge` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a "where" that is not met (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters runs from the Court's ruling on further arguments` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters runs from the Court's ruling on further arguments` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no request for further arguments
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters runs from the Court's ruling on further arguments` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a single application dealing with more than one matter
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters is still barred from running` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- request made, the Court has not ruled: the bar holds
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters is still barred from running` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Court affirmed, varied or set aside the decision: the bar has lifted
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters is still barred from running` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the Court certified that no further arguments are required: the bar has lifted
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters is still barred from running` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a single application dealing with more than one matter
#ASSERT `o 18 r 3(2)(d) the time for the appeal or the application for permission against the decisions on all matters is still barred from running` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no request: the bar does not arise

-- Rules 4 to 7
#ASSERT `o 18 r 4(1) the party may file another appeal for the application` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
