#ASSERT `o 18 r 6(3) interest is to be allowed for the time enforcement has been delayed by the appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless the lower Court or the appellate Court otherwise orders"
#ASSERT `o 18 r 6(3) interest is to be allowed for the time enforcement has been delayed by the appeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no delay in enforcement: outside "for such time as enforcement has been delayed"
-- Rule 7: appeal to AD or CA; AD or CA otherwise ordered under O 15 r 1(3); another provision provides otherwise
#ASSERT `o 18 r 7 the appeal must be heard in chambers` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 18 r 7 the appeal must be heard in chambers` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- open court under O 15 r 1(3): the Rule gives way and says nothing
#ASSERT `o 18 r 7 the appeal must be heard in chambers` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the Court has otherwise ordered under O 15 r 1(3) (marginal reading: see NOTES)
#ASSERT `o 18 r 7 the appeal must be heard in chambers` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- another provision provides otherwise

